st/size.test.ts:195:\t// S11 (TodoMVC ADVANCED) IS THE CORPUS'S NEW HEAVYWEIGHT ON BOTH AXES, and it\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:196:\t// is the first row in this table with NO ANGULAR TWIN - that lane refuses the\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:197:\t// scenario outright on its global-identifier ban, so `S11` exists in five\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:198:\t// `generated/` directories and not six.\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:199:\t// Against S10, the previous heaviest: 424/275 = 1.54x the physical lines and\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:200:\t// 1891/1262 = 1.50x the structural nodes. The two ratios agreeing to within 3%\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:201:\t// is the same reading S10's row made against S7 and it survives one size step\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:202:\t// further out: this emitter still pays no per-element tax that grows nodes\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:203:\t// faster than lines.\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:204:\t// WHAT THE NUMBER CANNOT SEE, recorded for the same reason S8's row records it.\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:205:\t// S11 is the first corpus scenario to write ONE CELL ON BOTH SIDES OF AN\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:206:\t// `await` - the optimistic update - and DEFECTS.md 12.2's functional-updater\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:207:\t// fold therefore DECLINES on both writes, leaving the post-suspension read in\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:208:\t// const-SSA form (`nextTodos.map(...)`) where the other four lanes read the\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:209:\t// live cell. That is a behavioural divergence at an identical size, so a budget\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:210:\t// could never catch it; only a served payload can.\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:211:\tS11: { physicalLoc: 424, structuralNodes: 1891 },\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:212:\t// S12 (the CODEX CLONE) IS THE CORPUS'S BIGGEST TEMPLATE AND NOT ITS BIGGEST\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:213:\t// EMISSION, and that inversion is the reading worth recording. Its template\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:214:\t// carries FIFTY-THREE hosts against S11's forty-one - the largest in the\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:215:\t// corpus by a third - yet it emits SMALLER on both axes: 386/424 = 0.91x the\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:216:\t// physical lines and 1760/1891 = 0.93x the structural nodes. The ratios agree\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:217:\t// to within 2%, so the emitter is not trading one axis for the other; the app\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:218:\t// simply has a different SHAPE. S11 is dense in HANDLERS (nineteen recorded\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:219:\t// events, several with a full list rebuild inside a `.map`), while S12 is dense\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:220:\t// in STATIC MARKUP - two tab pairs and two detail panes that are mostly literal\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:221:\t// rows. Emitted size tracks handler bodies, not host count, which is exactly\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:222:\t// what a per-element tax would NOT look like.\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:223:\t// WHAT THE NUMBER CANNOT SEE, recorded for the same reason S8's and S11's rows\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:224:\t// record it. S12 is the corpus's first scenario with THREE awaits in one\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:225:\t// handler, and its three post-suspension writes are chained through `const`s\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:226:\t// (`opened` -> `chunk1` -> `chunk2` -> `chunk3`) precisely so that this lane's\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:227:\t// const-SSA resume and the other three lanes' live-cell resume produce the SAME\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:228:\t// behaviour. That agreement is authored, not emitted - the divergence S11's row\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:229:\t// records is still there in the emitter, and a budget cannot see either half.\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:230:\tS12: { physicalLoc: 386, structuralNodes: 1760 },\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:231:};\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:232:\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:233:describe('honest emitted structure comparison', () => {\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:234:\ttest('measures the actual calibrated handwritten component bodies', async () => {\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:235:\t\texpect(await measureAll()).toEqual([\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:236:\t\t\t{\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:237:\t\t\t\tscenario: 'S1',\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:238:\t\t\t\treference: { physicalLoc: 39, structuralNodes: 161 },\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:239:\t\t\t\temitted: { physicalLoc: 41, structuralNodes: 183 },\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:240:\t\t\t},\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:241:\t\t\t{\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:242:\t\t\t\tscenario: 'S2',\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:243:\t\t\t\treference: { physicalLoc: 98, structuralNodes: 576 },\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:244:\t\t\t\temitted: { physicalLoc: 102, structuralNodes: 537 },\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:245:\t\t\t},\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:246:\t\t\t{\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:247:\t\t\t\tscenario: 'S3',\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:248:\t\t\t\treference: { physicalLoc: 102, structuralNodes: 407 },\npackages/frameworks/react/test/size.test.ts:249:\t\t\t\temitted: { physicalLoc: 84, struct