{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'for f in demos/{react-official,solid-official,qwik,svelte-official,vue-official,angular-official}/package.json; do echo \"$f\"; rg -n '\"'\\\"dev\\\"|port' \\\"\"'$f\"; done\nsed -n '\"'85,120p' README.md\nsed -n '115,175p' demos/react-official/src/App.jsx\nrg -n \\\"threeWayScenarios|six|official demos|ports\\\" scripts/e2e.mjs README.md demos/*/package.json | head -200\nls scripts\"","aggregated_output":"demos/react-official/package.json\n10:    \"dev\": \"pnpm copy-emitted && pnpm copy-todomvc-css && pnpm copy-shadcn-theme && node server\",\ndemos/solid-official/package.json\n10:    \"dev\": \"pnpm copy-emitted && pnpm copy-todomvc-css && pnpm copy-shadcn-theme && node server\",\ndemos/qwik/package.json\n10:    \"dev\": \"pnpm copy-emitted && pnpm copy-todomvc-css && pnpm copy-shadcn-theme && vite --port 5175 --strictPort\",\ndemos/svelte-official/package.json\n10:\t\t\"dev\": \"pnpm copy-emitted && pnpm copy-todomvc-css && pnpm copy-shadcn-theme && vite dev\",\ndemos/vue-official/package.json\n10:    \"dev\": \"pnpm copy-emitted && pnpm copy-todomvc-css && pnpm copy-shadcn-theme && node server\",\ndemos/angular-official/package.json\nBuilds both demo libraries (`demos/ui-kit` and `demos/composition-kit`, which\nhas cross-file imports, children, shared state, and element access with\ncleanup) into React 19 and Solid, runs them in a headless browser, and writes\na report under each demo's `receipts/` folder.\n\n## See It Yourself: Hydrate, Hydrate, Resume\n\nOne source. Three frameworks. Two activation models. The same behavior.\n\n```sh\npnpm install\npnpm demo\n```\n\nThat boots all three official demo apps — each through its own untouched\nframework scaffold, none of them a hand-rolled harness — and prints their URLs\nonce all three answer. Ctrl-C stops all three.\n\n| Demo  | URL                      | Activation | S1  | S2     | S3     |\n| ----- | ------------------------ | ---------- | --- | ------ | ------ |\n| React | <http://localhost:5173/> | hydrates   | `/` | `/s2`  | `/s3`  |\n| Solid | <http://localhost:5174/> | hydrates   | `/` | `/s2`  | `/s3`  |\n| Qwik  | <http://localhost:5175/> | resumes    | `/` | `/s2/` | `/s3/` |\n\nQwik's nested routes keep their trailing slash — its router normalises `/s2`\nto `/s2/`.\n\nThe three scenarios: **S1** a counter that renders once (`kit:2`, click, `kit:4`),\n**S2** a keyed to-do list (add, remove, reorder, clear), **S3** a form with\nevents and inputs.\n\n### One source, all the way down\n\nNothing in those three apps is hand-written per framework. Each column is\ngenerated from the column to its left.\n\n      <button type=\"button\" data-harness=\"release\" onClick={() => s8Gate.release()}>\n        release\n      </button>\n      <p data-harness=\"gate\">{ready === s8ResolvedGate ? 'open' : 'held'}</p>\n      <AsyncBoard ready={ready} onTrace={noTrace} />\n    </>\n  )\n}\n\n/**\n * Maps a request URL onto a scenario id. The stock create-vite SSR scaffold\n * already threads `req.originalUrl` into `render(url)`, so branching on it here\n * mirrors the Qwik demo's `/`, `/s2`, `/s3` routes without adding a router.\n *\n * @param {string} url\n * @returns {'s1' | 's2' | 's3' | 's4' | 's5' | 's6' | 's7' | 's8' | 's9' | 'todomvc' | 'todomvc-advanced' | 'codex'}\n */\nexport function scenarioFor(url) {\n  const path = String(url ?? '')\n    .replace(/^\\/+/, '')\n    .replace(/\\/+$/, '')\n  if (path === 's2') return 's2'\n  if (path === 's3') return 's3'\n  if (path === 's4') return 's4'\n  if (path === 's5') return 's5'\n  if (path === 's6') return 's6'\n  if (path === 's7') return 's7'\n  if (path === 's8') return 's8'\n  if (path === 's9') return 's9'\n  // THE FIRST APPLICATION, and the only path here that is not an ordinal. It is\n  // NOT part of the 6 x 9 three-way contract - `scripts/e2e.mjs` pins\n  // `threeWayScenarios` to the literal ['s1'..'s9'] - so this route is browsable\n  // only, which is exactly the sequencing the goal asked for.\n  if (path === 'todomvc') return 'todomvc'\n  // THE SECOND APPLICATION. Five lanes, not six - angular refuses S11.\n  if (path === 'todomvc-advanced') return 'todomvc-advanced'\n  // THE THIRD APPLICATION - the Codex clone. Five lanes emit it, four run its\n  // stream; angular has no route at all. Browsable only, like the two above.\n  if (path === 'codex') return 'codex'\n  return 's1'\n}\n\n/**\n * @param {{ url?: string }} props\n */\nexport default function App({ url }) {\n  switch (scenarioFor(url)) {\n    case 's2':\n      return <KeyedTodo seed={s2Seed} onTrace={noTrace} />\n    case 's3':\n      return <EventForm initial=\"hello\" onTrace={noTrace} />\n    case 's4':\n      return <NestedBoard seed={s4Seed} onTrace={noTrace} />\n    case 's5':\n      return <BranchBoard seed={s5Seed} onTrace={noTrace} />\n    case 's6':\n      return <WhitespaceBoard seed={s6Seed} label={s6Label} onTrace={noTrace} />\n    case 's7':\n      return <FormBoard seed={s7Seed} onTrace={noTrace} />\n    case 's8':\n      return <AsyncGate />\nREADME.md:86:has cross-file imports, children, shared state, and element access with\nREADME.md:121:| Scenario | You write                                             | Compiler records (IR)                                | Frameless emits                                           | Demo imports                                                            |\nREADME.md:129:itself only imports them.\nREADME.md:177:| **AI ports per framework** | An AI rewrites your component for each framework.                                         | It is a guess. It changes every run, it can quietly change behavior, and someone has to review every file for every framework after every change.                   |\nREADME.md:178:| **Hand-written ports**     | You maintain one codebase per framework.                                                  | N times the work, N times the bugs, and drift the moment one port gets a fix the others do not.                                                                     |\nREADME.md:230:| `packages/cli`              | Builds many files at once and writes build reports.                                                                                                                                                                   |\nscripts/e2e.mjs:28:// The official framework scaffolds. One shared IR, six emitters, two\nscripts/e2e.mjs:84:const threeWayScenarios = ['s1', 's2', 's3', 's4', 's5', 's6', 's7', 's8', 's9'];\nscripts/e2e.mjs:87:// it loads, so the official demos run boxes without depending on it themselves.\nscripts/e2e.mjs:434:// Five of the six only need their emitted components refreshed; Angular\nscripts/e2e.mjs:452:\tthreeWay[demo.framework] = await readThreeWayResults(demo, threeWayScenarios);\nscripts/e2e.mjs:457:for (const scenario of threeWayScenarios) {\nscripts/e2e.mjs:473:for (const scenario of threeWayScenarios) {\nscripts/e2e.mjs:499:\t`Three-way: ${officialDemos.length} demos x ${threeWayScenarios.length} scenarios, all observations equal`,\ncheck-citations.mjs\ncorpus-mutation.mjs\ndemo.mjs\ne2e.mjs\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
