{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"I found the emitter defect: one literal `0x00` byte is embedded in `src/emitter/index.ts` as a map-key separator. The launcher’s current readiness check accepts any status-200 body, starts all children before checking ports, and its exit sweep can only distinguish spawned children after the fact. I’m replacing those weak checks with positive lane/route body fingerprints plus a negative refusal probe, and making occupied-port handling happen before any spawn."}}
